ip -4 addr show | grep inet

		inet 127.0.0.1/8 scope host lo
		inet 172.30.1.2/24 brd 172.30.1.255 scope global dynamic noprefixroute enp1s0   ---> chose this preferable [ range: 172.30.1.200-172.30.1.220 ]
		inet 172.17.0.1/16 brd 172.17.255.255 scope global docker0
		inet 192.168.0.0/32 brd 192.168.0.0 scope global flannel.1
		
Apply the MetalLB manifest
	
		kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/metallb/metallb/v0.13.12/config/manifests/metallb-native.yaml

Create your actual IPAddressPool

	cat <<EOF | kubectl apply -f -
	apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
	kind: IPAddressPool
	metadata:
	  name: default-pool
	  namespace: metallb-system
	spec:
	  addresses:
	  - 172.30.1.200-172.30.1.220
	---
	apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
	kind: L2Advertisement
	metadata:
	  name: l2
	  namespace: metallb-system
	spec: {}
	EOF


Verify MetalLB is running

		kubectl get pods -n metallb-system

Watch for the EXTERNAL-IP allocation

		kubectl get svc -n nginx-ingress -w

Optional check: confirm the IPs are unused

		ping -c 2 172.30.1.200   [  If no reply → ✔ good.  ]
